{"baseRefName":"main","body":"## Summary\n- keep disabled plugin backends authoritative only when they have a version matching the request\n- fall back to the first enabled registry backend for versions that would require a new install\n- verify `mise install --dry-run` and `mise lock` select the enabled backend while an older plugin version remains installed\n\nRefs #12921.\n\n## Tests\n- `MBX_DISABLE=1 mise run lint-fix`\n- `MBX_DISABLE=1 mise exec -- cargo check --all-features`\n- `MBX_DISABLE=1 mise exec -- cargo test --bin mise cli::args::backend_arg::tests`\n- `MBX_DISABLE=1 mise run test:e2e e2e/backend/test_disable_backends`\n\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Codex; model: openai/unavailable; version: unavailable.*\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Changes core `BackendArg::full()` resolution for shorthand tools with disabled plugins and leftover install state; wrong matching could mis-route installs or lockfile backends.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> When `MISE_DISABLE_BACKENDS` blocks a plugin backend, **registry shorthand resolution** now considers the **requested version**, not merely whether any version was installed via that plugin.\n> \n> A disabled asdf/vfox plugin still wins for a version **already installed** through it; for a **new** version (or no version in the request), resolution falls back to the first **enabled** registry backend instead of staying pinned to the leftover plugin. `BackendArg` carries this via a new `requested_version` field, set from `with_registry_version` on every version-aware lookup while `registry_version` is only used when the registry entry has version-bounded backends.\n> \n> E2E coverage for `age` asserts `mise tool --backend`, `install --dry-run`, and `mise lock` pick `aqua:FiloSottile/age` for `1.3.1` while `1.2.1` remains on `asdf:age`.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit f2797ca844cfcca3c317319216fea2185c3f740b. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved tool version resolution when multiple backends are configured.\n  * Versions already installed through a disabled backend remain available through that backend.\n  * Other requested versions now resolve through the first enabled registry backend when appropriate.\n  * Lock files now accurately record the selected backend and platform after installation previews and lock updates.\n  * Registry-based version constraints are applied more consistently.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","headRefName":"codex/fix-disabled-backend-version-selection","title":"fix(backend): select enabled backend for uninstalled versions","url":"https://github.com/jdx/mise/pull/12927"}
